<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Province of Freedom</h1><p class="st-meta">1787 CE – 1789 CE · capital Granville Town</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived settlement of freed Black Londoners on the Sierra Leone peninsula, the first attempt at what became Freetown.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Province of Freedom grew out of the campaign by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granville-sharp">Granville Sharp</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/committee-for-the-relief-of-the-black-poor">Committee for the Relief of the Black Poor</a> to resettle impoverished Black people in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, many of them Loyalists from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American War of Independence</a>. About 400 settlers sailed in 1787 and landed in May on land obtained from local Koya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temne-people">Temne</a> rulers, where they founded Granville Town.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Sharp designed it as a self-governing community with elected leaders, including Richard Weaver, and a frankpledge system of mutual responsibility. In practice the settlers suffered from disease, poor harvests and the rainy season, and many died or left to work for slave traders on nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bunce-island">Bunce Island</a>. Relations with neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temne-people">Temne</a> chiefs were uneasy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1789 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temne-people">Temne</a> ruler known as King Jimmy burned Granville Town after a dispute. The survivors regrouped, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone-company">Sierra Leone Company</a> took over the project, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sierra-leone-colony-and-protectorate">Sierra Leone Colony and Protectorate</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a> in 1792.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/province-of-freedom.jpg" alt="Province of Freedom" width="320" height="297"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Province_of_Freedom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1787 CE – 1789 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Granville Town</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Richard Weaver</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Granville Town</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=province-of-freedom" aria-label="Province of Freedom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4351 1859 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Province of Freedom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M4634 2117h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4671 2115h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4671 2115h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Sierra Leone. <a href="/atlas?year=1788&amp;focus=province-of-freedom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
